      "writtenOn": "2022-11-04T14:04:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find the AuthFsTestRule very confusing. Why are so many of the members static? (That doesn\u0027t seem to be documented.)\n\nI know we only ever have one instance, but that\u0027s isn\u0027t a particularly good reason to use a Monostate.\n\nSo maybe we should fix it the other way, by making the members non-static.",
      "revId": "bb6a3a384107d5995b5e94111a8eac283e66f35e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bfe3e357_5d8ce8f6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-04T16:28:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AuthFsTestRule actually extracts the authfs tests setup/teardown part. The Host test did part of the setup inside a class setup and part as test setup, so when I extract a rule I preserved this[1]. Now the rule is used in both benchmark test and host test and the setup is a bit different. How would you like to improve it?\n\n[1] https://r.android.com/2162318",
      "parentUuid": "f990e80c_bc7ac7de",
      "revId": "bb6a3a384107d5995b5e94111a8eac283e66f35e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eec1e503_8d847188",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-04T16:48:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I see - so one wants to call methods from the static @BeforeClass, but the other one wants to do the same initialization for every test? And yet we use static variables even for the latter, which looks a little weird.\n\nI wonder if there should be some other class which encapsulates the current static state in the Rule. Then we can either create a static instance of that for the tests or multiple instances for the benchmarks. In each case we can feed the instance in to the Rule which can then store it as a normal member.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "bfe3e357_5d8ce8f6",
      "revId": "bb6a3a384107d5995b5e94111a8eac283e66f35e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a554ca2d_8af8fe4d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-07T15:59:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I thought about that approach initially, but there\u0027s another problem. Though the setup is neat, one needs class level setup and the other needs test level. There\u0027s also per test setup/teardown that\u0027s required in both tests[1] (e.g. like clearing the test directory). \nI made a quick test locally. If we make the rule in host test static, the per test setup/teardown won\u0027t work anymore.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/authfs/tests/common/src/java/com/android/fs/common/AuthFsTestRule.java;l\u003d246;drc\u003df31230fb18fa367a62f8815cfb896fb09b41d2cd",
      "parentUuid": "eec1e503_8d847188",
      "revId": "bb6a3a384107d5995b5e94111a8eac283e66f35e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57a66978_7e9abc8d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-07T16:35:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m suggesting having 2 different classes. The Rule would remain non-static, but would depend on another object, which would be static or not depending on the use case, and would take over the currently static functions \u0026 variables in the rule.",
      "parentUuid": "a554ca2d_8af8fe4d",
      "revId": "bb6a3a384107d5995b5e94111a8eac283e66f35e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
